From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Opsero <support@opsero.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:20:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] net: axienet: default to 1024 RX descriptors on MRMAC and HSE
 ports

None of the MACs without a PHY that this BSP drives has RX backpressure:
the MRMAC, the UltraScale+ CMAC and the 40G/50G subsystem (l_ethernet,
both XAXIENET_HSE) present RX AXI-Streams without tready. The AXI MCDMA
S2MM channel behind them silently discards a whole frame whenever the
RX descriptor ring has no free descriptor. The driver's default ring of
128 descriptors is refilled from NAPI; any scheduling gap longer than
~128 frame times (~15 us of 1500-byte frames at 100G, ~40 us at 40G)
therefore loses frames. The loss is invisible in the MAC and netdev
error counters and only shows up as TCP retransmits and as the MCDMA
S2MM packet-drop count (MCDMA base + 0x514).

Measured with the MRMAC on VCK190 + Quad SFP28 FMC (TCP host->board,
30 s): 10G 50415 retransmits with 128 RX BDs, 226 with 1024; 25G 73348
with 128, 3599 with 1024. The HSE ports use the same MCDMA ring code.

Default MRMAC and HSE ports to 1024 RX descriptors. The TX ring and all
other MAC types keep their defaults; "ethtool -G" still overrides the
value while the interface is down.

Memory cost per port with a 1500-byte MTU: 1024 x ~2 KiB RX skbs plus
1024 x 128 B coherent descriptors, i.e. ~2.1 MiB instead of ~0.26 MiB,
allocated only while the interface is up.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c
index 657d80c22578..0ad9aadbb775 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c
@@ -58,6 +58,11 @@
 
 /* Descriptors defines for Tx and Rx DMA */
 #define RX_BD_NUM_DEFAULT		128
+/* MRMAC / HSE (CMAC, l_ethernet) RX has no backpressure: the MCDMA S2MM drops
+ * whole frames whenever the RX ring has no free descriptor, so give those
+ * ports a deeper ring.
+ */
+#define RX_BD_NUM_NO_BP_DEFAULT		1024
 #define TX_BD_NUM_MIN			(MAX_SKB_FRAGS + 1)
 #define TX_BD_NUM_MAX			4096
 #define RX_BD_NUM_MAX			4096
@@ -5273,6 +5278,12 @@ static int axienet_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	lp->hse_leth = of_device_is_compatible(pdev->dev.of_node,
 					       "xlnx,l-ethernet-4.0");
 
+	/* Still adjustable with "ethtool -G" while the interface is down */
+	if (lp->axienet_config &&
+	    (lp->axienet_config->mactype == XAXIENET_MRMAC ||
+	     lp->axienet_config->mactype == XAXIENET_HSE))
+		lp->rx_bd_num = RX_BD_NUM_NO_BP_DEFAULT;
+
 	/* Setup checksum offload, but default to off if not specified */
 	lp->features = 0;
 #ifndef CONFIG_AXIENET_HAS_MCDMA
-- 
